      <iframe src="../../media/desmos/a47b5bb4ba783be55a7067b919f165f14dcc36ce.html" width="500" height="400"/><!--END ADD DESMOS INTERATIVE-->
      <note>
        <para>Building Character: Growth Mindset</para>
        <div class="os-raise-d-flex-nowrap os-raise-gap-1">
          <figure>
            <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
              <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_14_10_03.png"/>
            </media>
          </figure>
          
            <para>Compared to a fixed mindset, a growth mindset encourages you to embrace challenges, sustain effort, and try new strategies. Of course, no one embodies only a growth or fixed mindset; we are all a mixture of the two, and we can learn to recognize what triggers a fixed versus growth mindset. The brain is like a muscle—something you can strengthen.</para>
            <para>Think about your current sense of having a growth mindset. Are the following statements are true for you?</para>
            <list>
              <item>
          I truly believe that people can change.
       </item>
              <item>
          I can always change how intelligent I am.
       </item>
            </list>
            <para>Don’t worry if none of these statements are true for you. Developing this trait takes time. Your first step starts today!</para>
          
        
      </note>
    </section>
